   "s": "GICHSGFIN",
   "n": "GIC Housing Finance Limited",
   "cat": "Credit Rating",
   "when": "2026-09-19 10:37",
   "sent": "positive",
   "txt": "**1. Single Most Important Fact**\nCRISIL Ltd. has reaffirmed GIC Housing Finance\u2019s credit ratings at **CRISIL AA+/Stable** (for long-term bank facilities and existing NCDs) and **CRISIL A1+** (for short-term bank facilities and commercial paper), while assigning a **CRISIL AA+/Stable** rating to a new limit-enhanced NCD issue of Rs. 500 crore.\n\n---\n\n**2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated**\n*(Note: Financial performance metrics like Revenue/EBITDA/PAT are not part of this credit rating intimation.)*\n\n* **Long-Term Bank Facility (Rs. 8,100 cr.):** Re-affirmed at `CRISIL AA+/Stable`\n* **Short-Term Bank Facility (Rs. 1,000 cr.):** Re-affirmed at `CRISIL A1+`\n* **NCDs (Rs. 500 cr.):** Re-affirmed at `CRISIL AA+/Stable`\n* **NCDs (Rs. 430 cr., reduced from Rs. 1,030 cr.):** Re-affirmed at `CRISIL AA+/Stable`\n* **NCDs (Rs. 500 cr. - Limit Enhanced):** Assigned `CRISIL AA+/Stable` (New)\n* **Commercial Paper (Rs. 1,500 cr.):** Re-affirmed at `CRISIL A1+`\n\n---\n\n**3. Management Guidance / Outlook**\n* **Outlook:** CRISIL maintained a **\"Stable\"** outlook across all long-term facilities and NCDs.\n* No management guidance or operational forward-looking statements were included in the filing.\n\n---\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**\n* **No action required.** \n* Monitor the company\u2019s cost of borrowing and deployment of newly rated funds (Rs. 500 cr. enhanced NCDs) into loan book growth.\n\n---\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**\n**Neutral to mildly positive:** Reaffirmation of top-tier credit ratings (`AA+` and `A1+`) confirms stable balance-sheet strength and ensures continued access to debt markets at competitive interest rates."
  }
